 "notes": "One topic per option. The specification prints each option with a section letter and an option letter (AA-AD and BA-BE on Paper 1, AA-AC and BA-BD on Paper 2), so a topic ref is the paper number plus that code: 1AA America, 1840-1895 ... 2BD Restoration England. The body text prints Britain: Power and the people as 'BB'; the at-a-glance list and its place among the thematic studies make it AB, so it is 2AB. Subtopics are the option's Parts (Part one = .1), and each point is one content bullet in the order printed (2BC.1.2 = Elizabethan England, Part one, second bullet); a point's title is the bullet's own heading, the words before its first colon. The bullets are unnumbered in the specification. History is untiered: no Higher-only content. Skipped: Part four of each British depth study (2BA-2BD), the historic environment, because AQA names a different site each year."
}